 "notes": "MuDHI dielectric haloscope observed 90% CL upper limit on kinetic mixing chi vs dark photon mass. Curve traced from the magenta MuDHI curve in Fig. 11 of the v3 e-print (file Erratum_noLambda.png, the corrected/erratum version). Extracted by pixel analysis: axes calibrated from major ticks (x: col307=1eV, 844px/decade; y: row105=1e-7, 129.1px/decade); per-column lower edge of the magenta ink taken as the boundary of the excluded region, downsampled every 4th column (95 pts). Extracted minimum chi=6.81e-11 at m=1.61 eV/c2 matches the paper stated minimum 6.86e-11 at 1.61 eV/c2. Assumed local DM density 0.3 GeV/cm3 (App. A, eq A2); no rescaling applied. The limit is highly oscillatory (inverse of boost-factor spectrum); mass range ~1.12-3.09 eV/c2. The paper also shows a 15th-85th percentile boost-factor uncertainty band limit; the headline solid measured curve (measured thicknesses) is reported here.",
